PART 2: UNDERSTANDING CURLY BRACES IN JSX

================================================================================

What Do Curly Braces Mean?

Inside JSX, curly braces:

{ }


mean:

Evaluate this as a JavaScript expression.


They let you move from JSX markup into JavaScript expressions.

Simple Example

Without curly braces:

<h1>Hello name</h1>


Output:

Hello name


With curly braces:

const name = 'Alice';

<h1>Hello {name}</h1>


Output:

Hello Alice


================================================================================

WHERE CAN YOU USE CURLY BRACES?

================================================================================

1. Inside JSX Content
const title = 'My Book';

<h1>{title}</h1>


Output:

My Book

2. Inside JSX Properties
const id = 'book-1';

<div id={id}>
  Book
</div>

3. Normal JavaScript Does Not Need JSX Braces
const name = 'Alice';

console.log(name);


Here {} is unnecessary because this is normal JavaScript, not a JavaScript expression embedded inside JSX.

Quick Understanding
Location                 | Example
-------------------------|---------------------------
JSX Content              | <h1>{name}</h1>
JSX Property             | <div id={id}>
Event Handler            | onClick={handleClick}
Normal JavaScript        | console.log(name)
Literal JSX Text         | <h1>Hello name</h1>


