Type 2: Mathematical Expressions

================================================================================

export default function Calculator() {

  const price = 29.99;
  const quantity = 3;
  const tax = 0.1;

  return (
    <div>

      <p>
        Price per book: ${price}
      </p>

      <p>
        Quantity: {quantity}
      </p>

      <p>
        Subtotal: ${price * quantity}
      </p>

      <p>
        Tax: ${price * quantity * tax}
      </p>

      <p>
        Total: ${price * quantity * (1 + tax)}
      </p>

    </div>
  );
}

Calculations
Expression                   | Result
-----------------------------|---------
price                        | 29.99
quantity                     | 3
price * quantity             | 89.97
price * quantity * tax       | 8.997
price * quantity * (1 + tax) | 98.967


Output:

Price per book: $29.99
Quantity: 3
Subtotal: $89.97
Tax: $8.997
Total: $98.967


For currency-display code, formatting to two decimal places is normally preferable, but the values above preserve the lesson's original calculation output.

