Type 5: Ternary Operator - Conditional Rendering

================================================================================

Ternary syntax:

condition ? valueIfTrue : valueIfFalse


Example:

export default function BookStatus() {

  const isAvailable = true;
  const stock = 5;

  return (
    <div>

      <p>
        Status:
        {isAvailable
          ? ' Available'
          : ' Out of Stock'}
      </p>

      <p>
        Stock:
        {stock > 0
          ? ' ' + stock + ' copies'
          : ' No copies'}
      </p>

      <p>
        Price:
        {stock > 10
          ? ' $15.99'
          : ' $19.99'}
      </p>

    </div>
  );
}

Conditions
Condition       | True Result   | False Result
----------------|---------------|----------------
isAvailable     | Available     | Out of Stock
stock > 0       | 5 copies      | No copies
stock > 10      | $15.99        | $19.99


With the current values:

Status: Available
Stock: 5 copies
Price: $19.99


