Type 6: Array Methods - map()

================================================================================

map() is commonly used to transform array data into JSX elements.

export default function BookList() {

  const books = [
    {
      id: 1,
      title: 'The Great Gatsby'
    },
    {
      id: 2,
      title: '1984'
    },
    {
      id: 3,
      title: 'To Kill a Mockingbird'
    }
  ];

  return (
    <div>

      <h1>Books</h1>

      <ul>

        {books.map(book => (

          <li key={book.id}>
            {book.title}
          </li>

        ))}

      </ul>

    </div>
  );
}

Explanation
Code                  | Purpose
----------------------|--------------------------------------------
books.map(...)        | Processes every book
book                  | Current book object
<li>                  | Creates list element
key={book.id}         | Provides stable identity among siblings
{book.title}          | Displays title


Output:

Books

- The Great Gatsby
- 1984
- To Kill a Mockingbird


