Pattern 2: Conditional Rendering with &&

================================================================================

export default function BookStatus() {

  const isAvailable = true;

  return (
    <div>

      {isAvailable && (
        <p>
          This book is available!
        </p>
      )}

      {!isAvailable && (
        <p>
          This book is out of stock
        </p>
      )}

    </div>
  );
}

How && Works Here
Condition             | Result
----------------------|---------------------------------
isAvailable = true    | Show "available"
!isAvailable = true   | Show "out of stock"


Easy memory:

condition && JSX

TRUE
 ↓
Render JSX

FALSE
 ↓
Don't Render JSX


