Pattern 3: Looping Through Arrays

================================================================================

export default function BookList() {

  const books = [
    'Book 1',
    'Book 2',
    'Book 3'
  ];

  return (
    <ul>

      {books.map((book, index) => (

        <li key={index}>
          {book}
        </li>

      ))}

    </ul>
  );
}

Explanation
Code              | Purpose
------------------|-------------------------------------
books.map(...)    | Processes each array item
book              | Current book value
index             | Current array position
<li>              | JSX generated for each book
key={index}       | Key used in this simple example


For lists that can be inserted, deleted, reordered, or otherwise change dynamically, a stable data ID is generally preferable to the array index.

