PART 7: COMMON MISTAKES

================================================================================

Mistake 1: Forgetting Curly Braces

Wrong:

const name = 'Alice';

<h1>Hello name</h1>


Output:

Hello name


Correct:

const name = 'Alice';

<h1>Hello {name}</h1>


Output:

Hello Alice


================================================================================

Mistake 2: Using Statements Directly Inside JSX Expressions

================================================================================

JSX curly braces expect expressions.

This is invalid:

{
  if (isAvailable) {
    return 'Available';
  }
}


Also invalid directly in JSX:

{
  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    console.log(i);
  }
}


Use expressions instead.

Ternary
{
  isAvailable
    ? 'Available'
    : 'Out of Stock'
}

map()
{
  [1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map(i => (
    <li key={i}>
      {i}
    </li>
  ))
}

Expression vs Statement
Expression                     | Statement
-------------------------------|------------------------------
Produces a value               | Performs an action/control flow
name                           | if (...)
2 + 2                          | for (...)
getPrice()                     | while (...)
condition ? A : B              | switch (...)
items.map(...)                 | variable declaration statement


================================================================================

Mistake 3: Missing key in Lists

================================================================================

Wrong:

{books.map(book => (

  <li>
    {book.title}
  </li>

))}


Correct:

{books.map(book => (

  <li key={book.id}>
    {book.title}
  </li>

))}


key helps React identify sibling elements across renders.

================================================================================

Mistake 4: Overly Complex JSX Expressions

================================================================================

Harder to read:

{
  books
    .filter(b => b.price < 20)
    .map(b => b.title)
    .join(', ')
}


For more complex/reused logic, extract it:

const getAffordableBooks = () => {

  return books
    .filter(b => b.price < 20)
    .map(b => b.title);
};


JSX:

{getAffordableBooks().join(', ')}


Flow:

COMPLEX LOGIC
     ↓
EXTRACT TO FUNCTION
     ↓
FUNCTION RETURNS VALUE
     ↓
JSX USES RESULT


================================================================================

COMMON MISTAKES - QUICK TABLE

================================================================================

Mistake                | Avoid                    | Better
-----------------------|--------------------------|------------------------------
Variable as text       | Hello name               | Hello {name}
if inside JSX          | {if (...)}               | {x ? A : B}
for inside JSX         | {for (...)}              | {items.map(...)}
Missing list key       | <li>{item}</li>          | <li key={item.id}>
Complex JSX logic      | Big chained expression   | Extract function/variable
Unclear names          | x, y, t, a               | isAvailable, bookTitle
Unstable list identity | key={index}              | key={book.id}, when available


