TERNARY vs && - QUICK REVISION

================================================================================

Ternary                         | &&
--------------------------------|------------------------------------
Choose between two outputs      | Render something conditionally
Has true and false branches     | Commonly used for one-sided rendering
condition ? A : B               | condition && A


Example:

{inStock
  ? 'In Stock'
  : 'Out of Stock'}


Use when both outcomes matter.

Example:

{inStock && (
  <button>
    Buy Now
  </button>
)}


Use when content should appear only when the condition is truthy.

